# 0309 = 0305 + the rebased ACR3 BIST fix (0308b) + throughput axes.
#
# Cleanup (user decision): the CL-0306 (0x860/cfgnoflush) and CL-0307
# (ruby_txring_pa low ring) negative arms are deleted from the series; the
# ACR3 fix is rebased as patches/0308b-ruby-usb-acr3-bist.patch.
#
# New boot args (all defaults reproduce the 0308 steady state):
#   ruby_txgpd=512        TX bytes per GPD (64..16384)
#   ruby_txgpd_num=64     TX GPD slots in use (8..64; array stays 64)
#   ruby_inflight=16      TX in-flight cap (1..64, clamped to txgpd_num)
#   ruby_rxgpd_num=16     RX GPD slots in use (4..16; array stays 16)
#   ruby_rxslot=2         RX FIFO slot, (slot+1)*512 B (0..7)
#   ruby_rxbuf=512        RX GPD declared buflen (existing, 64..16384)
#   ruby_txslot=2         TX FIFO slot (existing; clamp tightened to 0..7)
# Banner gate: "RUBY USB: 0309 txgpd=%u txring=%u inf=%u ...".
#
# The 16 KB caps are the static buffer sizes (TX per-GPD payload 16 KB, RX
# per-GPD storage 16 KB); the ACM echo ring is raised 8 KB -> 32 KB so one
# 16 KB host write is not dropped.  Ring counts only tune downward in this
# CL; the vendor 144-slot rings would need dynamic allocation.
#
# RX safety: a transfer that fills exactly one ring lap makes RQCPR wrap to
# deq; the drain now recognises that full-lap shape and restarts a stopped
# queue with Q_START.  TX keeps one ring slot reserved (inflight <= n-1),
# so the TX drain cannot see a full-lap wrap.  The TX push also restarts a
# queue that stopped after draining (RESUME on a stopped queue is a no-op).
#
# Zero-build repack_cmdline changes every axis; defaults stay 0308.
#
# Default cmdline: config/0309-boot.cmdline (544 B; the axes stay at their
# code defaults, so zero-build repack_cmdline can append 1-4 test axes while
# staying under the 607-byte SWEETXNU cmdline field).
# Acceptance: default 8/8 + 60 s sustained echo + zero-build matrix over
# txgpd / txgpd_num / inflight / rxbuf / rxgpd_num / rxslot.
# patchset: a40f1997f3c05f7f3f1ce31dc5360dae6728be907aaa56075a1e22a61ac9d327
#           (290 files, computed locally from baseline-mirror)
KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA=1c81a450130c2325518ec87d107fd6e5d604c5a5e4dc88a356e2a77796e031c7
